    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32676": {
      "title": "University of Texas",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | LARC Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help LARC Supervisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07225P Position Title LARC Supervisor Functional Title Facility Resources Supervisor - Lab Animal Resource Center (LARC) Department Research Operations & Labs Salary Range up to $70,000 DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/10/2026 Posting Close Date 09/16/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 09/28/2026 Job Summary The Facility Resources Supervisor serves as a critical leadership position within the Lab Animal Resource Center ( LARC ) at UT Dallas. This role is responsible for overseeing daily facility operations, supervising husbandry and technical staff, and ensuring the highest standards of humane animal care, facility maintenance, and regulatory compliance. The supervisor supports the university’s growing biomedical research enterprise by facilitating efficient resource management, technical assistance to investigators, and effective collaboration with the IACUC , veterinarians, and research faculty. All activities within this position align with the Guide for the Care and Use of Laboratory Animals, IACUC policies, and federal, state, and institutionalregulations. Minimum Education and Experience High school diploma or GED . Five (5) years of basic animal care experience. Assistant Laboratory Animal Technician ( ALAT ) certification or ability to obtain within one (1) year of hire. A Certified Veterinary Assistant ( CVA ) credential or Certified Veterinary Technician ( CVT ) may be considered in lieu of the ALAT certification. Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education: Bachelor’s degree in Animal Science, Biology, Veterinary Technology, or a closely related field; or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Preferred Experience: Minimum 4–6 years of progressive experience in laboratory animal care and vivarium operations, or clinical setting. Experience in a university or academic research setting. Familiarity with vivarium/clinical management software, environmental control systems, and/or IACUC protocol management tools (e.g., Cayuse). Knowledge of additional research models or specialized housing (e.g., quarantine procedures). Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Lead, supervise, and mentor a team of LARC husbandry technicians, animal care staff, and support personnel. This includes recruitment support, training and development (including AALAS certification pathways), performance evaluations, scheduling, and disciplinary actions as needed. Oversee all aspects of daily vivarium operations, including animal husbandry, cage processing, sanitation, waste management, and environmental monitoring (temperature, humidity, ventilation, lighting, noise levels). Assist LARC leadership in maintaining facility resources and inventory: procure and maintain adequate supplies of feed, bedding, PPE , cleaning agents, and specialized equipment; develop cost-effective procurement strategies and maintain accurate records. Provide hands-on technical support to researchers, including animal handling, restraint, basic procedures, breeding support, weaning, and health surveillance. Ensure accurate and timely documentation, including animal census reports, health records, breeding logs, facility maintenance logs, and compliance reports for IACUC , leadership, and regulatory agencies. Serve as a key point of contact for facility access, researcher orientation/training, animal ordering/imports, and conflict resolution in coordination with the LARC management, coordinator and research administration. Respond promptly to after-hours, weekend, and holiday emergencies involving animal welfare, facility systems failures, or security concerns (participating in on-call rotation). Collaborate with veterinary staff, IACUC , and the Office of Research and Innovation on protocol compliance, facility inspections, program audits, and continuous improvement initiatives. Promote and enforce occupational health and safety standards, including proper use of PPE , biosafety practices, and participation in the UTD - UTSW Occupational Health Program. Identify opportunities for operational efficiencies, equipment upgrades, process improvements, and enhanced animal welfare practices (e.g., environmental enrichment). Perform other duties as assigned to advance the mission of the LARC and support UT Dallas research objectives. Strong leadership, communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills with a service-oriented approach toward researchers and colleagues. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, database/record-keeping systems, and basic facility management tools. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical and Working Conditions Ability to lift and carry up to 30-pounds; perform repetitive motions; stand, walk, and bend for extended periods. Work in a controlled environment with exposure to animal allergens, chemicals, noise, and varying temperatures. Must be willing to work flexible hours, including early mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays as required for animal care continuity. Participation in an on-call rotation for emergencies. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Remote work not available for this position. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training BCBS PPO Medical insurance – 100% paid for full-time employees PPO and DHMO Dental Insurance Plan – PPO plans include ortho benefits Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan – defined benefit plan offering lifetime annuity upon retirement Voluntary Retirement Plan Options – additional savings opportunities with Tax-Sheltered Annuity Plans and Deferred Compensation Plans Dental/Vision/AD&D Paid time off Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break Fertility Benefits All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. If you are looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Look no further! Join our team! Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
