    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32688": {
      "title": "Learning Specialist II (JSOM)",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Learning Specialist II (JSOM) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Learning Specialist II (JSOM) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07235P Position Title Learning Specialist II (JSOM) Functional Title Department Management Salary Range $51,000, DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/11/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Summary The University of Texas at Dallas has an excellent job opportunity for individuals looking to join our team as a Learning Specialist II in the Naveen Jindal School of Management ( JSOM ). The Learning Specialist II provides advanced instructional support and program development in business communication, professional development, student success, and AI-enhanced learning. This role supports undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students through workshops, individual coaching, classroom integration, and cross-campus collaboration. The position reports to the Director of Professional Development and plays a key role in advancing student success by integrating communication training with career readiness, academic support, and emerging technologies such as generative artificial intelligence. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree with three (3) years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience Master’s degree in English, Communication, or a related field. Experience working in higher education, particularly in student success, academic support, writing centers, graduate education, career services, or professional development programs. Experience supporting undergraduate and graduate students. Experience designing, delivering, and assessing workshops, training programs, curricula, and educational resources for diverse student populations. Experience coordinating programs, communications, or services across multiple stakeholders while managing competing priorities and deadlines. Experience with Canva, presentation software, social media platforms, and other tools used for student engagement, outreach, and program promotion. Experience supporting executive-level DBA students with dissertation writing, formatting, publication processes, and academic communication. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs) Demonstrated knowledge of professional communication principles, including business writing, presentation skills, networking, public speaking, LinkedIn branding, personal marketing, and career readiness strategies. Knowledge of assessment design in the areas of Second Language Acquisition and/or English as a Second Language, specifically for evaluating the written and spoken English language skills of graduate doctoral students. Knowledge of phonetics and phonology and the ability to evaluate spoken English to determine whether additional resources or support may be beneficial in preparing individuals to teach management courses in an English-language classroom. Familiarity with generative AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot, Gemini) and the ability to support the ethical and effective use of AI in academic and professional settings. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills with the ability to effectively engage student populations and collaborate with faculty, staff, and stakeholders. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and work independently while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide general group and individual coaching to undergraduate and graduate students on business communication, professional development, student success resources, and using AI for academic and professional success. Provide individualized support to PhD and DBA students on dissertation formatting, research paper reviews, submission requirements, and publication standards. Provide coaching and assessments to PhD and DBA students on key professional communication skills, including speaking (networking, small talk, conferences, public speaking) and writing for public-facing academic materials (e.g., LinkedIn posts, presentations, personal websites) Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Work Notice: Work will be performed on-site and in person. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits BCBS PPO Medical Insurance Options – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees AD&D Insurance Dental & Vision Plan Options Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Fertility Benefits Paid time off All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
