    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32716": {
      "title": "University of Texas",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Internal Auditor III Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Internal Auditor III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07246P Position Title Internal Auditor III Functional Title Department Audit and Advisory Services Salary Range $72,000, DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/14/2026 Posting Close Date 09/25/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Summary The University of Texas at Dallas Audit and Advisory Services Department is seeking a collaborative, analytical, and motivated Internal Auditor III to join its team. In this role, you will conduct assurance and advisory engagements, investigations, and other projects that provide objective and independent evaluations in support of the department’s vision and mission to deliver risk-based, objective assurance, advice, insight, and foresight to management in the areas of governance, risk management, and internal control. You will serve as a project leader or collaborate as a member of project teams while contributing to the University’s commitment to effective governance and accountability. Performs other duties as directed by audit leadership. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in an applicable field. At least three (3) years of related professional experience. PREFERRED : Having and maintaining at least one of the following credentials Certified Public Accountant ( CPA ), Certified Internal Auditor ( CIA ), Certified Information Systems Auditor ( CISA ), or Certified Fraud Examiner ( CFE ). Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in accounting, management, information technology, or another business-related field aligned with the responsibilities of the position. Four years of professional experience in auditing or a business-related field aligned with the responsibilities of the position, including at least one year of auditing experience. Possession and maintenance of at least one of the following professional certifications: Certified Public Accountant ( CPA ), Certified Internal Auditor ( CIA ), Certified Information Systems Auditor ( CISA ), or Certified Fraud Examiner ( CFE ). Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Internal Auditor III is responsible for effectively and efficiently performing the following duties and responsibilities: Conducts and Leads Engagements Conducts engagement-level risk analyses and planning to define project objectives, scope, and methodologies. Develops audit programs for routine audits and/or project plans to achieve engagement objectives. Collects, researches, analyzes, and observes appropriate information, data, and evidence to accomplish project objectives. Compiles data from the University’s information systems and other internal and external sources. Conducts interviews, questionnaires, and surveys. Utilizes audit management software to perform audit work. Uses appropriate sampling techniques, artificial intelligence (AI), and data analytics tools to enhance audit processes and achieve engagement objectives. Engagement Documentation Prepares thorough, well-organized, and self-explanatory working papers that support conclusions reached. Identifies issues and assists in developing recommendations. Drafts observations and recommendations based on work performed. Project Management and Quality Assurance When leading projects, coordinates the work of team members and provides guidance and instruction as needed. Performs the initial review of work papers prepared by other team members. Monitors time budgets and target completion dates for assigned projects. Evaluates the effectiveness of the audit process at the conclusion of each engagement. Coordinates follow-up audit procedures for outstanding audit issues. Client Relations Leads entrance and exit conferences. Identifies and develops issues and collaborates with audit clients to reach sound and effective recommendations. Keeps clients informed of project status, barriers to progress, and potential issues to help ensure there are no surprises regarding observations and recommendations. Conducts professional communications to understand processes and obtain audit evidence. Collaborates with campus stakeholders to support audit activities, including building and maintaining positive client relationships. Internal Communications Keeps audit leadership informed of the status of audit work, potential issues and proposed solutions, and client relations. Report Development Drafts engagement reports and evaluates clients’ written responses to recommendations. Other Duties and Responsibilities Maintains and continually develops competencies required by the Global Internal Audit Standards by participating in professional education and training as directed by audit leadership and in accordance with professional development plans. Travels occasionally to off-site locations for audit work and professional conferences. Works infrequent evening or weekend hours, as needed. Participates in and volunteers with professional auditing organizations. Assists audit leadership with meetings, training, and other team events. Performs other projects and duties as assigned by audit leadership. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Remote Work Notice: After the probationary period, this role may be eligible for a hybrid (partly remote/partly in office) work schedule, subject to business need and manager approval. Must be located within the DFW Area and have the ability to be on campus with 24 hours of notice. A UT Dallas Remote Work Agreement will be required within 14 days after approval. What We Can Offer: UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits BCBS PPO Medical Insurance Options – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees AD&D Insurance Dental & Vision Plan Options Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Fertility Benefits Paid time off All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32719": {
      "title": "University of Texas",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Lead PeopleSoft DBA Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Lead PeopleSoft DBA Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07233P Position Title Lead PeopleSoft DBA Functional Title Department Shared Services Salary Range Commensurate with experience Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Multiple Locations Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/15/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 10/05/2026 Job Summary The Lead PeopleSoft DBA works with all stakeholders from technical and functional units to deploy, implement and maintain Enterprise PeopleSoft application systems (PS) and Oracle databases ( DBA ). The main purpose is to oversee PS and DBA system and architecture configuration; performing PS and DBA patching procedures while providing support to direct staff; assigning resources to support PS and DBA technology roadmaps for PS systems ( HCM ; FMS ; IH; CS) and related DBA support for ancillary systems like CTRLM , Hyperion, PHIRE , and OBIA databases. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree and 4 years of related experience or associate’s degree and 6 years of related experience or high school diploma and 8 years of related experience. Preferred Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree and 6 years of related experience or associate’s degree and 8 years of related experience or high school diploma and 10 years of related experience. Preferred Qualifications: 2 years Supervisory experience Comprehensive PeopleSoft Administration: 10+ years extensive experience as a PeopleSoft Backend Administrator (version 9.0+) on an on-premise Linux platform, including installation, configuration, patching, performance tuning, and troubleshooting across multiple PeopleSoft products and PeopleTools versions Technical Architecture & Infrastructure: Proficient in designing, developing, and maintaining technical architecture and distributed processing environments to support PeopleSoft implementations, including Internet Architecture, WebLogic, Tuxedo, and batch servers Integration & Security Expertise: Skilled in PeopleSoft messaging, integration tools (IB, API , FTP ), certificate management, authentication, load balancing, encryption, and system security, ensuring robust and secure PeopleSoft environments Advanced System Management: Experienced in capacity planning, system cloning, container technologies, search and insights tools, and evaluation/implementation of new PeopleSoft functionalities, with proven ability to debug complex infrastructure and application issues Extensive Oracle Database Administration: 10+ years’ experience as an Oracle DBA (Oracle 11g/12c/19c) on an on-premise Linux platform Replication, Migration & Backup: Deep expertise in Oracle database replication (GoldenGuard), migrations, upgrades, backup and recovery ( RMAN ), and database auditing, with strong skills in automation (scripting, backup, monitoring) and monitoring ( OEM , custom, third-party tools) Performance & Capacity Planning: Proficient in capacity and performance planning, tuning at both database and O/S layers (memory, CPU , network, storage), and optimizing Oracle databases on VMWare for high throughput Development & ETL Processes: Experienced in Oracle development ( SQL , PL/ SQL ), ETL / ELT processes ( API , SQL*Loader, External Tables), and implementing/managing Oracle databases for ancillary systems ( OBIA , ODV , Hyperion, PHIRE , CTRLM ) Holistic Technical Leadership & Innovation: Demonstrates strong organizational, teamwork, and communication skills, excels in guiding and managing PSDBA team efforts, and champions automation, artificial intelligence, and data-driven solutions (including AI coaching, log analysis, and data visualization). Brings expertise in higher education business practices, technical tool evaluation, and collaboration across all organizational levels to foster continuous improvement and operational excellence Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Functions: Contribute expertise and execution of assigned Team Lead tasks including: Develop, manage and collaborate on standard practices and processes within the PeopleSoft Administration and DBA ( PSDBA ) framework Mentor other PS Administrators and DBAs; building a sense of community within the team Actively promote the value of PeopleSoft and Oracle DB administration throughout the organization Prepare periodic reports on project status, progress, risks, deadlines and resource requirements for specific track Support project objectives by leveraging project management methodologies Provide direction, support and feedback within the PSDBA team Perform team lead duties including scheduling, reporting to management, supervising, delegating and prioritizing workloads Resolve issues within and across teams Provide recommendations for process/procedure improvements Leverage technology to help reduce manual tasks and continually improve processes Build and maintain lasting relationships with all technical and business stakeholders Contribute independent subject matter expertise and execution of assigned including: Incident management and resolution Request fulfillment Problem management root cause analysis Assisting with review and analysis of workload and future demand for PSDBA team Planning and monitoring system state and exception metrics Improving and altering business and technical processes Creating, improving and managing automation platforms and processes Ongoing analysis of PSDBA system state and services Development of detailed deployment, validation and QA plans to ensure positive product deployment Collaborate and share knowledge including: Demonstrating functionality and expertise to educate internal team and relevant stakeholders as necessary Documenting and sharing tools, tips and knowledge within and across teams Provide content/develop communication to stakeholders as necessary Posting and reviewing internal documentation for PSDBA team Develop requirements for documentation of technical customizations and/or third-party integrations from Pillar and/or campus as related to PSDBA tasks Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong critical thinking, analytical skills and problem resolution; ability to quickly interpret and gather requisite information; process oriented and solid hand-off skills Successfully engage in multiple initiatives simultaneously. Work independently with users and under direction of project managers to plan, schedule, and deliver projects Drive and challenge stakeholders on their assumptions of how they will successfully execute their plans. Demonstrate strong analytical and product management skill, including a thorough understanding of how to interpret customer business needs and translate them into application and operational requirements. Deliver the highest quality service through performance, results, and ownership approach Supports team management in work assignments and project planning Supports team management in direct associate goal setting and performance reviews Physical Demands and Working Conditions May work around standard office conditions. Repetitive use of a keyboard at a workstation. Some travel may be required. Uses standard office equipment. Requires occasional evening or weekend hours. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. Position location will be discussed during the interview process. Location can be Fort Worth, TX or Richardson, TX. Hybrid remote work environment available. A UT Dallas Remote Work Agreement is required upon employment. Must have the ability to be on Richardson campus within 48 hours of notice. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32721": {
      "title": "Senior Director of AccessAbility Resource Center",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Senior Director of AccessAbility Resource Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Senior Director of AccessAbility Resource Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07238P Position Title Senior Director of AccessAbility Resource Center Functional Title Senior Director of AccessAbility Resource Center Department AccessAbility Resource Center Salary Range $120,000, Depending on Qualifications Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/11/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/01/2027 Job Summary Job Summary The Senior Director of the AccessAbility Resources Center ( ARC ) is a strategic leadership role responsible for overseeing university-wide accessibility services for students and ensuring compliance with federal and state regulations. Reporting to the Vice President for Academic Success & Innovation, this position serves as the University’s primary subject matter expert on ADA compliance, leading a dedicated team to provide comprehensive accommodations that enable students with disabilities to meet their academic potential. The Senior Director balances operational efficiency with long-term planning, focusing on removing barriers to education, modernizing accommodation workflows, and partnering with the Office of Information Technology, Educational Technology Services, and the Center for Teaching and Learning to advance digital accessibility standards. In addition to managing operations, the Senior Director works closely with faculty and academic leadership to provide professional development and advocate for student needs. The ideal candidate will demonstrate exceptional collaboration skills and advanced communication acumen, enabling them to build trust across a wide spectrum of stakeholders, including students, faculty, staff, and senior leadership, while navigating complex and sensitive conversations with empathy and clarity. The candidate will skillfully cultivate collaborative partnerships, promote a campus-wide culture grounded in respect, shared accountability, and drive strategic initiatives that meaningfully strengthen student engagement, access, and belonging. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree with ten years of work experience in related field. Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Fourteen or more years of progressively responsible experience in a related field. Prior experience supervising and leading a complex team. Five years or more of experience in higher education. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Lead the creation and execution of a strategic vision for the ARC , aligning accessibility goals directly with major institutional initiatives for student success. Use assessment data to evaluate the impact of services on student success and graduation rates, ensuring continuous improvement and responsiveness to student needs, while identifying campus-wide bottlenecks and forecasting future resource requirements. Serve as the primary subject matter expert on federal and state regulations ( ADA , Section 504/508, Fair Housing Act). Partner with Legal Counsel and Risk Management to interpret legislation, mitigate institutional liability, and guide leadership on best practices. Direct the daily operations of the ARC , including the intake process, exam administration, and assistive technology. Oversee the departmental budget and personnel, ensuring scalable workflows to handle increasing caseloads. Collaborate with academic leadership to transition the university from a retroactive accommodation model to a proactive Universal Design for Learning ( UDL ) framework. Develop and deliver training for faculty on accessible course design and navigating complex accommodation scenarios while maintaining academic integrity and respecting academic freedom. Partner with the Office of Information Technology ( OIT ) and Educational Technology Services to ensure digital assets meet WCAG 2.1 AA standards. Consult with Facilities Management on capital projects to ensure physical environments exceed minimum code requirements. Lead, mentor, and evaluate a diverse team of accessibility professionals. Foster a high-performance culture grounded in empathy, professional growth, and operational excellence. Work closely with students to ensure their feedback informs the development of ARC services, ensuring a consistent and inclusive experience across all aspects of university life, while actively fostering their self-advocacy skills and managing expectations around reasonable accommodations. Mediate complex situations between students and faculty, utilizing diplomatic persuasion to build buy-in for accessibility as a shared campus responsibility rather than solely a legal mandate. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Required Skills & Competencies Demonstrated understanding of best practices for supporting student success, retention, and access in a research university setting. Proven ability to mentor and develop professional staff, encouraging growth and fostering a collaborative, high-performance team culture. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills, with the ability to engage with a wide range of stakeholders—including students, faculty, and executive leadership—to foster an environment of respect. Deep understanding of recent and emerging laws governing accessibility in higher education ( ADA , Section 504/508). Ability to exercise sound judgment, tact, discretion, and integrity when handling confidential information and sensitive conversations, backed by strong conflict resolution and de-escalation skills. Connection to national initiatives and trends related to accessibility, inclusive educational technologies, and Universal Design. Experience relating to budget oversight and resource allocation. Ability to act as a change agent, anticipating demographic and technological shifts, and leading without direct authority to drive proactive practices across academic micro-cultures. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training BCBS PPO Medical insurance – 100% paid for full-time employees Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Dental/Vision/AD&D Paid Time off Fertility Benefits About Us UT Dallas is a top public research university located in one of the nation’s fastest-growing metropolitan regions. Our seven schools offer more than 140 undergraduate and graduate programs, plus professional certificates and fast-track programs. Our student body is 31,000 strong, reflecting students from over 100 countries and a multiplicity of identities and experiences. UT Dallas is committed to graduating well-rounded members of the global community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Official Transcripts Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32714": {
      "title": "University of Texas",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Audit and Advisory Services Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Audit and Advisory Services Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07244P Position Title Audit and Advisory Services Manager Functional Title Department Audit and Advisory Services Salary Range $100,000, Depending on Qualifications Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/14/2026 Posting Close Date 09/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Summary The University of Texas at Dallas Audit and Advisory Services Department is seeking an experienced, collaborative, and strategic Audit Manager to join its team. In this role, you will plan, lead, and supervise audits, advisory engagements, investigations, and other special projects that support the University’s commitment to effective governance, risk management, and internal controls. As a member of a small audit department, the Audit Manager serves as both a strategic leader and a hands-on contributor, exercising sound professional judgment while maintaining independence and objectivity. This position manages multiple engagements simultaneously, supervises audit staff and interns as assigned, and collaborates with stakeholders across the University to provide valuable insight and recommendations. The Audit Manager communicates engagement results and recommendations to management and governance bodies through the Chief Audit Executive ( CAE ) and performs other duties as assigned by audit leadership. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in an applicable field. Six (6) total years of related professional experience, to include at least three (3) years of auditing experience. Three (3) years of related supervisory experience. Professional and supervisory experience will be counted concurrently. Position requires having and maintaining at least one of the following credentials Certified Public Accountant ( CPA ), Certified Internal Auditor ( CIA ), Certified Information Systems Auditor ( CISA ), or Certified Fraud Examiner ( CFE ). PREFERRED : Three (3) or more years of auditing experience in an institution of higher education, a state or federal agency, or a large professional services firm. Preferred Education and Experience Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities Plan, perform, and manage risk‑based assurance engagements in accordance with the Texas Internal Auditing Act, Global Internal Audit Standards, and internal audit departmental policies and procedures. Lead audits with varying degrees of complexity, including financial, operational, compliance and other engagements. Conduct engagement‑level risk assessments and develop or review audit programs. Perform audit testing, evaluate internal controls, and document sufficient, reliable evidence. Review workpapers for accuracy, completeness, and conformance with professional standards. Draft audit reports and coordinate with management to confirm factual accuracy and obtain appropriate corrective action plans. Perform follow‑up procedures to assess implementation and effectiveness of agreed‑upon actions. Escalate significant risks, control deficiencies, or governance concerns to the CAE in a timely manner. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Remote Work Notice: After the probationary period, this role may be eligible for a hybrid (partly remote/partly in office) work schedule, subject to business need and manager approval. Must be located within the DFW Area and have the ability to be on campus with 24 hours of notice. A UT Dallas Remote Work Agreement will be required within 14 days after approval. What We Can Offer: UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits BCBS PPO Medical Insurance Options – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees AD&D Insurance Dental & Vision Plan Options Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Fertility Benefits Paid time off All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32725": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Administrative Assistant II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Assistant II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07204P Position Title Administrative Assistant II Functional Title Department Graduate Education Salary Range $45,000 DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/15/2026 Posting Close Date 09/19/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date Job Summary The Administrative Assistant provides essential administrative, operational, and customer‑service support to the Office of Graduate Education. Reporting directly to the Business Manager, this role supports procurement, scheduling, event coordination, financial processes, and daily office operations that ensure the smooth functioning of graduate programs and student services. The position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks in a fast‑paced academic environment. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree and five years of office administration or project management experience including two years at an Administrative Assistant I level or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Education and Experience Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Provide comprehensive administrative support to the Office of Graduate Education, including scheduling meetings, taking meeting minutes, managing calendars, conference room reservations, and handling correspondence with students, faculty, and external constituents. Assist in coordinating graduate program events, including student activities, department meetings, and facilitating room and resource access. Assist with purchasing processes, travel and hotel arrangements, and reimbursement submissions. Serve as the primary point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and visitors, offering information and directing inquiries appropriately. Assist in preparing reports, presentations, and other documents to support program initiatives. Support budget tracking and account reconciliation across multiple cost centers. Coordinate office communications, including email updates, website content revisions, and other communication needs as they arise. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Must be able to remain in a stationary position for long periods of time. The person in this position must occasionally move about inside the office to access file cabinets, office machinery, etc. Constantly operates a computer and other office productivity machinery, such as a calculator, copy machine, and computer printer. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information A remote work schedule is not available for this position. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training BCBS PPO Medical insurance – 100% paid for full-time employees PPO and DHMO Dental Insurance Plan – PPO plans include ortho benefits Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan – defined benefit plan offering lifetime annuity upon retirement Voluntary Retirement Plan Options – additional savings opportunities with Tax-Sheltered Annuity Plans and Deferred Compensation Plans Dental/Vision/AD&D Paid time off Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break Fertility Benefits All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. If you are looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Look no further! Join our team! Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please rate your skill level in using Microsoft Excel. None Beginner Intermediate Advanced * Do you have experience running front desk operations for a high traffic office?  If so, how many years? (Open Ended Question) * How many years of work experience in a higher education environment do you have? None Less than two years Two to five years Five to seven years More than seven years * Please describe any/all experience related to this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Relevant URL Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32717": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Assistant Athletic Trainer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Athletic Trainer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please apply online and attach cover letter, resume and 3 references. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07239P Position Title Assistant Athletic Trainer Functional Title Assistant Athletic Trainer Department Athletics Salary Range $55,000 - DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/14/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Summary The University of Texas at Dallas seeks an experienced and energetic athletic trainer who will, with the scope of licensure and legal boundaries, provide education, assessment, treatment and prevention services for athletic-related injuries and illnesses to assigned student-athletes, coaching staff, and members of the Athletic Department. The individual will assist in the day-to-day management of the athletic department’s sports medicine operation and provide effective delivery of athletic training services. Minimum Education and Experience •A bachelor’s degree from an accredited university in Athletic Training, Physical Education, or a related field is required. •Must possess a current and valid State of Texas Athletic Training license OR be eligible to immediately obtain this licensure. •Must be certified in First-aid, CPR and AED use. •Southwest Athletic Trainers Association ( SWATA ) member if applicable •BOC License Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience Master’s degree in Athletic Training, Sports Medicine, Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Physical Therapy, or a related field. One (1) year or more of athletic training experience in a collegiate, professional, secondary school, or similar athletic setting. Experience providing injury prevention, evaluation, treatment, rehabilitation, and return-to-play services for athletes. Experience coordinating medical coverage for practices, competitions, and team travel. Experience working collaboratively with physicians, healthcare providers, coaches, administrators, and student-athletes. Experience maintaining electronic medical records and implementing injury prevention, rehabilitation, or health education programs. Active participation in professional athletic training organizations such as NATA or SWATA . Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs) Knowledge of athletic training principles, sports medicine practices, emergency care procedures, and NCAA Division II regulations. Strong clinical skills in injury assessment, treatment, rehabilitation, and return-to-play decision-making. Ability to coordinate care and communicate effectively with student-athletes, coaches, parents/guardians, healthcare providers, and University personnel. Ability to maintain accurate, confidential, and compliant medical records and documentation. Strong interpersonal, organizational, time management, and problem-solving skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with stakeholders. Ability to exercise sound judgment, professionalism, and discretion when handling sensitive information. Ability to work independently, manage multiple priorities, and function effectively as part of a team. Proficiency with electronic medical record systems and standard business software. Ability to maintain required certifications, licensure, and professional competencies throughout employment. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities Comply with all applicable University policies and procedures, as well as NCAA , conference, and professional athletic training regulations, standards, and ethical guidelines. Represent the University professionally at practices, competitions, team travel, meetings, conferences, and community events. Assist with the daily operations, organization, and maintenance of athletic training facilities and equipment. Coordinate and provide comprehensive athletic training services for assigned sports, including injury prevention, evaluation, treatment, rehabilitation, practice coverage, event coverage, and team travel support. Deliver education and counseling to student-athletes regarding injuries, illnesses, treatment plans, and overall health and wellness. Maintain accurate, current, confidential, and compliant medical records and documentation. Serve as a liaison between student-athletes, team physicians, healthcare providers, coaches, and athletic department personnel to ensure continuity of care. Coordinate referrals and medical treatment plans with physicians and other healthcare professionals as appropriate. Communicate effectively with student-athletes, parents/guardians, coaches, athletic department staff, and sports medicine personnel regarding health and participation status. Educate coaches and athletic department staff on First Aid, CPR , AED usage, and Emergency Action Plans. Foster positive working relationships with athletic department leadership, coaches, student-athletes, faculty, staff, and campus partners. Participate in professional development activities and remain active within the athletic training profession. Maintain all required professional certifications, licenses, and credentials throughout employment. Demonstrate knowledge of and adherence to NCAA rules and regulations. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer or Director of Athletics. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Demands and Working Conditions Ability to work extended hours, including early mornings, late evenings, weekends, and holidays during athletic seasons. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds. Ability to travel on buses or vans for extended periods. Ability to stand outdoors for prolonged periods. Outdoor sports assignments may require working in hot, cold, or other varying weather conditions. Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team. Ability to adapt to changing schedules and operational needs. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Work will be performed on-site and in person. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits BCBS PPO Medical Insurance Options – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees AD&D Insurance Dental & Vision Plan Options Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Fertility Benefits Paid time off All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. If you are looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Look no further! Join our team! Special Instructions Summary Please apply online and attach cover letter, resume and 3 references. Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your highest degree level: None Associate's Bachelor's Master's Juris Doctor PhD or equivalent Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
