    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32756": {
      "title": "University of Texas",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Plumber Journeyman Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Plumber Journeyman Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07229P Position Title Plumber Journeyman Functional Title Department Facilities Management Salary Range $55,000 - $65,000 ($26.44-$31.25/hourly) Depending on Qualifications Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/16/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 10/12/2026 Job Summary To provide journeyman level skill in the installation and review of all types of plumbing systems; provide skills in the area of plumbing, electrical maintenance/repair to plumbing equipment; responsible for performing tasks in a specific area. Install and repair all plumbing in new construction or remodeling. Frequently responsible for the training and oversight of less skilled workers. Maintains a flexible work schedule including being on-call for occasional nights and weekends. Minimum Education and Experience High school diploma, GED or equivalent. Journeyman plumber license in the State of Texas. 3-5 years of related experience. Must have a valid Texas Driver’s license and acceptable driving record. Preferred Education and Experience Vocational/Technical Diploma Some College/Associate’s Degree in related field TCEQ Backflow Prevention Assembly Tester OSHA 10-Hour Training Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Performs service calls and work orders submitted by departments within the University, work could be performed off ladders, roof tops, or scaffolding. Performs preventative maintenance on all plumbing systems. Oversees training of less skilled workers while performing tasks. Troubleshoots plumbing system problems following detailed operational and maintenance procedures of existing and new plumbing systems installations. Surveys buildings and performs maintenance on equipment in a multi-trade working environment.  Maintains a clean and safe work environment.  Perform all work in accordance with best safety management practices. Maintains records and prepares reports on repairs and services according to university and regulatory requirements. Works from written and verbal instructions. Other duties as assigned. Must possess and maintain a valid Texas Driver’s License and an acceptable driver rating as established in Policy: UTS157 Section 2.5.4. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Work Notice: Work will be performed on site and in-person. May be required to report to on-site work location during campus closure. May be required to report to on-site work location during inclement weather. What we have to offer: We offer an employee-friendly work environment with a comprehensive benefit package including: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training Medical insurance – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability Retirement Plan Options Paid time off Paid Holidays All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. About UT Dallas The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to graduating well-rounded members of the global community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. A collection of people, ideas and perspectives is crucial to our vision and mission. UT Dallas is a place where members of the community are welcomed, treated fairly, and encouraged to their pursuit of excellence. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32749": {
      "title": "Senior Director of University Unions",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Senior Director of University Unions Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Senior Director of University Unions Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07243P Position Title Senior Director of University Unions Functional Title Senior Director of University Unions Department Student Union Salary Range $100,000 - DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/16/2026 Posting Close Date 09/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 12/01/2026 Job Summary The Senior Director of University Unions provides visionary leadership and strategic oversight for the administration, operations, and programs of the University Unions. This position leads the planning, development, implementation, and assessment of facilities, services, and initiatives that support and enhance the holistic student experience and the broader UT Dallas community. This role is responsible for setting and upholding high standards of excellence in the areas of policy implementation, delivery of quality services, revenue generation, assessment, facility maintenance and renovation, and student development. As a highly visible campus leader, this individual plays a key role in fostering collaboration and alignment within the Division of Student Affairs and across the university. This position is also responsible for the comprehensive fiscal management of a complex departmental budget exceeding $5 million, including the development and execution of sound financial strategies that ensure sustainability and growth. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree with ten years of work experience in related field. Preferred Education and Experience Master’s degree in public affairs, higher education administration, college student personnel, or other relevant academic concentrations 10+ years of professional experience in a higher education environment 6+ years of directly supervising professional staff members 6+ years of experience with budget creation and implementation 8+ years of experience managing operations of multiple large facilities in a college environment Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Leadership: Perform comprehensive administrative and supervisory oversight for all University Unions facilities, programs, and services, representing an annual operation exceeding $5 million across approximately 13 cost centers funded by three distinct student fees. Facilitate the hiring, training, and management of professional employees with general supervision of full-time staff and student employees in three different areas. Ensure that the more than 7,000 annual events and programs scheduled through University Unions reservations meet the expectations and needs of the university community. Provide strategic leadership and guidance in the following areas: University Unions operations and event services, reservations, student life programs ( SUAAB ), gaming & esports, revenue generation, facility maintenance, repair and replacement (R&R), budgeting, information technology (IT), capital construction, long-term planning, and assessment. Oversee safety initiatives for over 200 current professional staff (and 200 additional new union and success center staff) that work within the Student Union, Student Services Building, and Student Services Addition, ensuring regular communication, training, drills, and the Office Suite Monitor program. Facility Operations: Lead planning for facility and operational improvements, including major repairs and construction, renovations, and coordinate university partnerships for the successful opening of the Student Union-Student Success Center in January 2027. Supervise the following University Unions controlled facilities: Student Union (120,000 sq. ft.), Student Union-Student Success Center (369,000 sq. ft.), Student Services Building (70,000 sq. ft.), Student Services Addition (70,000 sq. ft.), and Comets LANding Gaming and Esports Center (15,000 sq. ft.). Additional outdoor locations such as the Margaret McDermott Mall, Chess Plaza, and the SU Green, along with significant outdoor space connected to the Student Union-Student Success Center; totaling approximately 644,000+ square feet. Collaborate closely with campus partners, including (but not limited to) the Office of Budget and Finance, Procurement Services, Human Resources, Facilities Management, Risk Management, the Offices of Undergraduate and Graduate Education, Provost’s Office, and Student Affairs. Serve as an active member of the Division of Student Affairs Leadership Team and Dean of Students Board of Directors, contributing to divisional and institutional initiatives and policy development. Advance university and divisional strategic goals related to student engagement, belonging, and retention. Student Engagement: Provide leadership, direction, and general supervision to the Gaming & Esports Program, which consists of a robust competitive esports program, along with the oversight of a 15,000 sq. ft., state-of-the-art gaming and esports center. Oversee the Student Union Activities and Advisory Board ( SUAAB ), which coordinates over 50 campus programs annually. Provide executive oversight of the STELLAR Student Employee Initiative , in collaboration with the University Career Center, to enhance the professional development of Student Union employees. This initiative ensures student employees engage in meaningful career development experiences, gain transferable career-readiness competencies, and can effectively articulate those skills in future professional contexts. These efforts will extend to all additional student employees hired for the forthcoming Student Union–Student Success Center. Work with registered student organizations and sponsored student groups to promote event planning, engagement, and success within University Union spaces. Attend various student organization functions, campus programs, and division and other meetings that pertain to the mission and operation of the University Unions department and division of Student Affairs. Maintain active dialogue with students and staff, applying a student development lens to decision-making while positively promoting the image of the department, division, and university. Fiduciary Responsibilities: Prepare and administer the annual operating budget. Authorize expenditures of departmental funds and other funds across student fees accounts and self-generated revenue streams totaling $2-3 million in non-salary expenditures annually. Lead efforts to secure sponsorships, partnerships, and donor contributions to advance priorities for the department and Division of Student Affairs. This includes solicitation, engagement, and converting of internal and external stakeholders. Additional Responsibilities: Serve as a lead delegate for the Dean of Students in the implementation and enforcement surrounding free speech and expression policies. Work with various campus stakeholders to apply interpretations to various violation scenarios Attend scheduled events and activism activities to ensure safety and student awareness of potential policy violations Monitor annual University Commencement Ceremony and semesterly Graduation Ceremonies for policy compliance Serve on the Speech and Expression Resource Team ( SERT ) through the DOS which is responsible for providing education and direction to students who are participating in expressive activities Represent University Unions and Student Affairs on standing university committees such as the Accessibility Committee, Auxiliary Services Committee, University Facilities Committee, University Safety Committee, and ad-hoc executive planning committees for large campus events such as Homecoming, Commencement After-Party, and Weeks of Welcome. Continue to position the University Unions department as the “pulse of campus”, leading event planning and campus community engagement efforts. Collaborate with division leadership on assessment and marketing strategies to enhance visibility and impact. Lead emergency response and critical incident planning, including drills and staff preparedness initiatives. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Preference may be given to internal candidates. Standard working hours for this position will be 8am-5pm Monday – Friday with occasional night and weekend obligations. Remote Work Notice: After the probationary period, this role may be eligible for a hybrid (partly remote/mostly in office) work schedule, subject to business need and manager approval. Must be located within the DFW Area and have the ability to be on campus with 24 hours of notice. A UT Dallas Remote Work Agreement will be required within 14 days after approval. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training BCBS PPO Medical insurance – 100% paid for full-time employees PPO and DHMO Dental Insurance Plan – PPO plans include ortho benefits Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan – defined benefit plan offering lifetime annuity upon retirement Voluntary Retirement Plan Options – additional savings opportunities with Tax-Sheltered Annuity Plans and Deferred Compensation Plans Dental/Vision/AD&D Paid time off Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break Fertility Benefits Remote Work Options – approved by department All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. If you are looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Look no further! Join our team! Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
