    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32752": {
      "title": "IT Support Specialist III",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | IT Support Specialist III Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help IT Support Specialist III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07164P Position Title IT Support Specialist III Functional Title Video Conferencing Specialist - TEAMS Support Department Information Technology-Office of the CTO Salary Range $58,854 Annually Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/16/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 10/12/2026 Job Summary This position is responsible for resolving issues related to in-room video conferencing equipment failure, physical malfunction and software configurations and conduct root cause analyses to improve processes and trend reoccurring issues to improve service. The Specialist will coordinate and lead IT stewardship of AV, Teams, and Zoom technology across conference center events. The position is primary on-site technician with the knowledge and skill set to fix 99% of issues in rooms, must have the ability to troubleshoot multimedia room integrated appliances to include, A/V device configuration, projectors, microphones, PTX video camera, digital whiteboards/annotation devices, integrated audio-conferencing digital sound processors, etc. This position will operate at the convergence of a/v conferencing, networking, and endpoint (computers/mobile) interoperability. Minimum Education and Experience Associate’s degree and four (4) years of related experience or an equivalent combination of related education and experience may be considered. Preferred Education and Experience 2 – 3 + years of managing AV VC environments. Must be responsive, efficient, and have excellent customer interaction. Experience with Teams Management Portal. Experience working with Senior Executive Staff. Ability to multitask in fast paced environment. Ability to troubleshoot in the field when needed, and conduct diagnostics to successfully problem-solve. Has a mindset that can help gather data and build reports about the trajectory of the AV/ V C environment Collaborative. Basic knowledge of enterprise networking fundamentals. Knowledge of troubleshooting PC, MAC and Linux common desktop problems. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Troubleshoot issues related to in-room video conferencing equipment failure, physical malfunction and software configurations and conduct root cause analyses to improve processes and trend reoccurring issues to improve service. The Specialist will coordinate and lead IT stewardship of AV, Teams, and Zoom technology across conference center events. Stay abreast of software and hardware involved in the management and implementation of modern A/V conferencing equipment with a focus on Microsoft Teams. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Remote Work Eligibility Statement Remote Work Not Available Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
